Meetings gain a lifecycle owner: `POST /meetings` (V19) takes a required `managed_by` field (`"wire"`, `"google_calendar"` or `"outlook"`, echoed in meeting responses; immutable after creation, not part of updates). `google_calendar`- and `outlook`-managed meetings can only be created, updated, deleted, link-refreshed and have invitations changed by calendar-integration (OAuth) callers; Wire clients (cookie/token with a connection) get `403 managed-by-calendar`. Meeting mutation routes now accept OAuth bearer callers (connection header is optional), enabling pure-bearer clients such as the calendar add-on.

Calendar-managed creates additionally carry `calendar_event_id` and `calendar_id` (both persisted, immutable; `calendar_id` is echoed in meeting responses). Every create/mutation of a calendar-managed meeting must present the `Z-Client: Calendar` request header and must not set calendar fields on wire-managed requests — violations return `400 invalid-op`. Creating a calendar-managed meeting on a deployment whose license does not cover calendar integration returns `403 id-feature-error`.
